    "name": "ProtSub-derived physicochemical distance",
    "source": "Jia, K. & Jernigan, R.L. (2021). New amino acid substitution matrix brings sequence alignments into agreement with structure matches. Proteins 89(6):671-682. DOI: 10.1002/prot.26050",
    "description": "Pairwise amino-acid distance derived from the ProtSub log-odds substitution matrix (Jia & Jernigan 2021, structure-aware) via the normalized form d(i,j) = (s(i,i) + s(j,j))/2 - s(i,j). Range approximately 0 (identical) to 15 (most dissimilar). NOTE: ProtSub is derived from MSAs of proteins encoded by the standard genetic code; it therefore falls under the Di Giulio (2001) tautology caution as a test of code optimality. Used as a structure-aware code-dependent robustness check, not as a primary physicochemical scale.",
    "symmetric": true,
    "conversion": "d(i,j) = (s(i,i) + s(j,j))/2 - s(i,j)",
    "caveat": "Code-dependent (MSA-derived). See Di Giulio (2001), J Theor Biol 208:141-144."
